Subject: [PATCH] Number boxes that can be written freely; backup folds to one
 line; restore updates the same draft
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

decisions.md 78:
- the title size box kept "২" because an empty box jumped back to 23 and
  Bangla digits were not taken. The number boxes (text and title size,
  table rows and columns) now keep what is written: a whole value inside
  the limits is used at once, anything else goes back to the last good
  value when the box is left (Enter leaves, Esc puts it back); Bangla
  digits work; − + in Settings.
- Settings → App → Backup folds to one line showing the last backup; open
  or closed is remembered on this device; back from Google it is open.
- restoring no longer makes "(ব্যাকআপ থেকে)" copies: the same draft (same
  id, from any device) is updated when the backup's state is newer and
  left as it is when this device's is; the other state is kept in the
  draft's version history. The open draft is saved first and reloaded if
  it was updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
